	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Type 'kill {query}' in Alfred to search running processes and terminate the selected one with the kill command.

Usage:
  kill chrome           - search processes whose name contains "chrome"
  kill node:server      - filter node processes whose args contain "server"
  kill -p 3000          - kill the process listening on TCP port 3000

Requires Node.js (Homebrew or system install).
Inspired by: https://github.com/ngreenstein/alfred-process-killer</string>
